{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_jev_playground", "label": "Jev Playground (weekly benchmark repo)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L1-L29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every week the author builds something real with Jev and publishes the numbers. Week 01, lead triage: Jev routed 90% of leads correctly at 366 ms and $0.04 per thousand against Sonnet 5's 78% at 2.6 s and $3.01. Week 02, deal risk from an AckDB activity ledger: every setup caught all 8 at-risk deals, and Jev did the whole ledger in 7.3 s for $0.0023 with one false alarm."}, {"id": "readme_typesafe_ai", "label": "TypeSafe AI (Jev vendor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L3-L6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_jev_typed_decision_model", "label": "Jev typed decision model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L6-L9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Send it state and typed questions and it returns a choice, a score, or a probability with a confidence attached. There is no text output. Input bills at $42 per billion tokens and output is free, since the output is a label and a number."}, {"id": "readme_decisions_vs_writing_split", "label": "Decisions vs writing split", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L11-L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whether Jev beats Claude is the boring question. The useful one is which steps of a real workflow are decisions and which are writing, and what happens to latency and cost when a frontier model stops doing the decisions. Week 01 gives the judgments to Jev and the email to Sonnet, and the MCP tools return labels and leave the writing to the agent."}, {"id": "readme_house_rules", "label": "House rules for the benchmarks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L31-L60", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rules the author holds the benchmarks to, and the reason the numbers come out lower than the ones in launch posts."}, {"id": "readme_hand_written_answer_key", "label": "House rule: the answer key is written by hand", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L36-L39", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If a model writes the labels, scoring that model against them measures self-agreement and quietly penalises every other model for disagreeing. Every label is hand-written against a published rubric you can argue with."}, {"id": "readme_shared_prompt_spec", "label": "House rule: both sides get the same words", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L41-L43", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The prompts are generated from one shared spec file. Jev gets the criteria as typed questions and Claude gets the same strings rendered as text, so nobody gets a hint the other did not get."}, {"id": "readme_fix_the_unfair_thing", "label": "House rule: fix the unfair thing even when it helps the other side", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L45-L49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Week 01 started with Claude burning 1,800 thinking tokens and 22 seconds per lead because the CLI turns thinking on by default, and turning it off took Claude to 2.6 s. Prompt caching was billed at full price until caught. claude_runner.py applies every Claude-favouring correction because a benchmark that only corrects in one direction is not worth publishing, and CLAUDE.md asks for each fix to be written down."}, {"id": "readme_measure_the_network", "label": "House rule: measure the network, not just the model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L51-L54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Jev's first call from the author's laptop looked like 970 ms: about 600 ms was the TLS handshake and about 290 ms was round trip time, leaving roughly 80 ms of model work. Every latency number says which is which."}, {"id": "readme_publish_the_failures", "label": "House rule: publish the failures", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L56-L57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every raw response is committed, including the wrong ones. If a number looks too good, read results/raw/."}, {"id": "readme_say_where_the_other_thing_wins", "label": "House rule: say where the other thing wins", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L59-L60", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Jev cannot write an email, and week 01 proves it by asking the live API for a text answer and showing the HTTP 400."}, {"id": "readme_sample_size_caveat", "label": "Sample-size caveat (60 leads, 20 deals, one laptop)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L79-L88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each week runs from one laptop in one place on one afternoon on a small hand-labelled set: 60 leads in week 01, 20 deals and 73 events in week 02. Accuracy is roughly plus or minus 8 points at 90% on 60 cases, and one deal is five points on 20. Cost numbers are the solid ones, since they are token counts against published rates. Take the shape of the result, not the third decimal place."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "readme_jev_typed_decision_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L6-L9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_typed_decision_model", "target": "readme_typesafe_ai", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L6", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "readme_decisions_vs_writing_split", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L11-L14", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_week_01_lead_triage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L20", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "week_02_deal_risk_readme_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L21", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "mcp_server_readme_using_this_from_an_agent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L25-L29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "readme_house_rules", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "mcp_server_readme_uv_inline_dependencies", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L75-L77", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "readme_sample_size_caveat", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L79", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_rules", "target": "readme_hand_written_answer_key", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L36", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_rules", "target": "readme_shared_prompt_spec", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L41", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_rules", "target": "readme_fix_the_unfair_thing", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L45", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_rules", "target": "readme_measure_the_network", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L51", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_rules", "target": "readme_publish_the_failures", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L56", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_rules", "target": "readme_say_where_the_other_thing_wins", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L59", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_hand_written_answer_key", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_rubric_rubric", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L38-L39", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_hand_written_answer_key", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_src_build_dataset_leads", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L36-L39", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_hand_written_answer_ke